# resources_gap_listed_twice: Each kind (a private buffer, a shared buffer, a private heap and a buffer in it, a normal texture, a two-plane Depth32Float_Stencil8 texture) listed twice in one exec. The shared buffer is discarded by 63 first, so that it needs a prepare. The first entry prepares each, the second finds it prepared: a copy out of each shows the guest bytes, paged in once. Then an exec writes each, every entry listed twice with invalidateGuest + synchronize (flags 6): each is synchronized once and its guest pages show the write. Then an exec writes each with invalidateGuest only (flags 2), and 53 names every one twice: the second synchronize of each finds its guest copy valid. In the service the buffers and the heap are detach resources over guest memory (CPU-paged), whose writes are in guest memory at once.
